  "findings": [
    "All four terminal fixtures resume a copy of the same state at FcuOperationEx 0x8008249c, with return address 0x8001437c, op 5 sector 0xa00 count 4, and no spare pointer. The source is the same 2048-byte extended-header buffer in every case.",
    "With zero statuses, the original caller frees the extended staging buffer, reads 256 sectors at sector 0, requests erase of block 0, and programs 256 sectors at sector 0 with 16 spare bytes. The read fixture returns the complete captured source of the earlier aggregate block-zero request. The final program reuses the same spare bytes.",
    "Original 0x80014874 changes only primary-buffer offsets +0x39c through +0x39f from little-endian 0xffffffff to 10, the first successful physical block of the section-2 extended header. Independent reconstruction from the captured primary source reproduces the full 131072-byte output SHA-256 ce8b5a7ef4d8d173b014dd27f085c1b326b998ab842044f59a03ebf30518e038.",
    "After the final op 5 succeeds, the original caller requests frees for the block map and primary buffer, then invokes the native ready callback at 0x80019390. Its return 1 is transformed by the original 0x80014d80 and 0x80014d88 sequence into BurnNand return 0. The trace ends at the restored caller sentinel without another storage request.",
    "An injected status 7 at the extended write, primary read or primary write results in native return 1 and no ready call. The failed read emits neither erase nor primary write. The trace records exact free calls, including null pointer arguments on these error paths. In the extended-write failure no free request for the extended staging buffer appears before return."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The finalization cases use one exact original-VEX snapshot after the earlier all-success aggregate main case. That main case supplies outcome and map effects in place of real block programming and comparison.",
    "The primary read uses the captured data and spare from the first aggregate program request. It models a successful read of those bytes and does not establish persistence on NAND.",
    "Storage statuses and pool behavior are fixtures. Free call arguments and software status are observed; allocation lifetime beyond this function, physical writes, hardware cache operations and actual camera update remain outside the replay."
  ],
